From: gt510 <gt510@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] software_isp: faster contrast autofocus

Autofocus took ~6 s: the statistics (and so the focus measure) were only
computed every 4th frame, every lens step waited two of them, and every
scan swept all 12 coarse and ~8 fine positions.

- Compute the statistics every frame; SwIspStats::focusValid marks them for
  autofocus while SwIspStats::valid (AGC, AWB) keeps its every-4th-frame
  cadence, so exposure and white balance behave as before.
- Wait for lens settling by frame number (settle frames after the move).
- Stop the coarse sweep once the measure has fallen below stopRatio of the
  best twice, refine with a parabola through the best coarse position and
  its neighbours, and check three fine positions around it.
- Refocus on a scene change after changeFrames frames of lasting change.
---
